    "title": "Connect actions and means",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-serial-actions-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Connect actions and means",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "For one subject, link going somewhere with the action done there, or 用 + tool with the action performed using it. A state with 着 can describe what accompanies movement. Keep the actor shared rather than silently switching who performs the actions.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我去学校学习。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ qù xuéxiào xuéxí 。",
                "meaning": "I go to school to study.",
                "audio": "e8ba1f85576a8e4a733d22e43a97a02b02d13dc4fd2aeff4e2b8b322af97ffdc"
              },
              {
                "text": "我用笔写字。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ yòng bǐ xiě zì 。",
                "meaning": "I use a pen to write characters.",
                "audio": "4379d348265cbffa0822f151a0e5e54f22ffacf3d97ff17998c779e3583b05db"
              },
              {
                "text": "他拿着一本书走进房间。",
                "pinyin": "tā ná zhe yī běn shū zǒu jìn fángjiān 。",
                "meaning": "He walks into the room holding a book.",
                "audio": "827cf4d53461db0530580dfbce9926ba9863e2560e6bd69be8d10c26384848f2"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
